nThe `Fit Content` docs for `RichTextLabel` say this:\n> If `true`, the label's minimum size will be automatically updated to fit its content, matching the behavior of Label.\n\nI just wanted to point out that a `Label`  with any `Autowrap Mode` enabled will exhibit the same vertical resize behavior as the first video in the original post above (the old, apparently unintended behavior of `RichTextLabel`). Is an autowrapping `Label` expected to behave differently compared to an autowrapping `RichTextLabel` with `Fit Content` enabled?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3895174410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]